course: dictionary
lesson: 2714
title: Dimension
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dimension is a measurement in one direction, like length, width or height. The dimensions of something are its size. When you measure a box, its length, width and height are its dimensions.
explain: Read the context. «The dust lying thick on everything … the cheerless, deserted look of the long-neglected house, and its narrow, meagre dimensions» shows a house left alone for years. Dust and neglect suggest it is run down, so its dimensions are its size. Meagre is a clue too: it means small and poor.
explain: A dimension can also be a side of something, like a problem or a feeling: «a new dimension» means another side to something. In a story, another dimension can be a different world. Ask yourself: is this word about a measurement, or about a side? Swap in a simple word, such as "size" or "side", and check the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A dimension is a measurement in one direction, such as length, width or height.
fact: A 2D shape has two dimensions: length and width.
fact: A 3D shape has three dimensions: length, width and height.
fact: The dimensions of something are its size, so you find them to work out area and volume.
fact: In stories, another dimension means a different world or reality.
exercise: In maths, how many dimensions does a 2D shape have? | *Two: length and width | One | Four | Three: length, width and height
exercise: What are the dimensions of something? | Its name and age | Its colour and smell | Its owner | *Its length, width and height, which is its size
exercise: In a story, what does another dimension mean? | *A different world or reality | A bigger box | A shape with four sides | A very long word
test: Which shape is 3D? | A square drawn on paper | A flat circle | A line | *A cube
test: What does meagre mean in «its narrow, meagre dimensions»? | Shiny and new | *Small and poor | Large and grand | Dark and wet
exam: A room is 4 metres long and 3 metres wide. Which word means these measurements of the room? | room | long | *dimensions | metres
